s or 2s, and potentially allows me to seize the initiative to play my QQQ triplet with the 6 as a kicker.\n\nReason: The current play is a single 8. I have single cards 6, K, and A. My strategy is to use the 6 as an attachment for the QQQ triplet (Triplet with single), but I need the lead to play that. Playing the King attempts to win the lead or force high cards from opponents. It is more efficient than playing the Ace (which should be saved for higher threats) and maintains my hand structure better than breaking the pair of 9s.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦K"]}'}
