ainst a player with 2 cards, and there is a chance they might lead a small pair (like 33) or that the higher pairs are broken up. Discarding the single 6 gives the best chance of survival.\n\nReason: Keeping a small single (6) as the last card is a losing strategy because opponents will block it with high cards once they see I have only one card left. Playing the 6 first clears the weakest card and keeps a pair (99) in hand, which has a better chance of winning if the opponents lead a small pair or lack higher pairs.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦6"]}'}
